Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.50,0:00:02.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}From Peking University and Google,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.67,0:00:06.81,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CITransNet is a context-integrated transformer for auction design.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.89,0:00:10.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It maximizes seller revenue while staying incentive-compatible,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.92,0:00:12.83,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}discovers asymmetric solutions,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:12.91,0:00:16.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and generalizes to auction sizes it never saw during training.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.17,0:00:22.66,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A classic problem in auction theory is designing a mechanism that maximizes the seller's
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.74,0:00:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}revenue while staying incentive-compatible.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.46,0:00:30.56,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Myerson solved the single-item case in 1981, but the multi-item case remains open,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.64,0:00:34.23,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and prior deep methods assume fixed or symmetric auctions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:34.61,0:00:36.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Real auctions are richer.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:36.24,0:00:37.86,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In e-commerce advertising,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.94,0:00:41.84,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}many bidders compete for many ad slots described by features,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.92,0:00:45.43,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and every round has a different number of participants.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.51,0:00:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}We need an architecture that absorbs context and handles varying auction sizes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.97,0:00:53.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The paper makes two contributions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:53.19,0:00:59.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It extends the RegretNet framework to the contextual setting and proves a sample-complexity bound.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:59.57,0:01:04.51,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}And it introduces CITransNet, permutation-equivariant over bids and contexts,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:04.59,0:01:06.92,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}not restricted to symmetric auctions,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:07.00,0:01:10.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with a parameter count independent of auction scale.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.69,0:01:14.19,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CITransNet takes three inputs: the bidding profile, bidder-contexts,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:14.27,0:01:17.78,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and item-contexts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:17.86,0:01:21.36,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It embeds contexts with bids into a representation per bidder-item pair,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:21.44,0:01:24.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}then passes it through transformer interaction layers that mix a global average with row and column transformers,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:25.02,0:01:28.52,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}staying permutation-equivariant.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:28.60,0:01:32.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A final layer outputs allocations and payments,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.19,0:01:35.69,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with zero-regret enforced during training.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.07,0:01:38.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}They evaluate on nine synthetic settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.82,0:01:41.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Three single-item cases, A through C,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:41.29,0:01:44.90,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}have known Myerson-optimal solutions as a sanity check.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.98,0:01:50.59,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The other six, D through I, are multi-item auctions up to five bidders and ten items,
Dialogue: 0,0:01:50.67,0:01:53.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the largest size in the auction-design literature.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:54.32,0:01:56.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Results come in two parts.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:56.24,0:02:01.94,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On single-item settings, CITransNet nearly recovers Myerson's optimal revenue,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:02.02,0:02:05.93,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}0.593 against 0.594, with regret below one thousandth,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.01,0:02:08.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}while context-blind baselines fall short.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.05,0:02:11.49,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the harder multi-item settings,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:11.57,0:02:16.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}it beats the Item-wise Myerson baseline in all six configurations,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.45,0:02:18.74,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}with gains reaching ten percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.12,0:02:20.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}To isolate why it works,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:20.70,0:02:28.24,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}the authors replace the transformer layers with RegretNet's fully-connected and EquivariantNet's equivariant layers,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.32,0:02:30.87,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}giving CIRegretNet and CIEquivariantNet.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.95,0:02:34.62,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Both still get context, yet earn less revenue everywhere,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:34.70,0:02:37.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}pinning the gain on the transformer layers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:37.53,0:02:40.21,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Removing context hurts even easy settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.59,0:02:43.33,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}A few numbers capture the impact.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.41,0:02:50.18,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}On the single-item benchmark, CITransNet reaches 0.593 versus the optimal 0.594.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:50.26,0:02:57.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}In the three-bidder ten-item setting it earns 6.872 against Item-wise Myerson's 6.509,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:57.61,0:03:01.98,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}and one continuous-context margin nears ten percent.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:02.06,0:03:05.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}It wins all six multi-item settings.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.44,0:03:10.53,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}The takeaway: context as a first-class input unlocks better learned auctions.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.61,0:03:15.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}CITransNet is near-optimal, asymmetric when needed, and incentive-compatible.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.78,0:03:22.35,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H00FFFFFF&}Its size-independent parameter count lets one trained model transfer to auction sizes it never saw.
